zebkit: build the Chrome DevTools Protocol endpoint into WebKit.framework

The macOS counterpart of 2005. The endpoint's sources are zebkit's own and
live in src/cdp, outside this tree; scripts/fetch-upstream.sh links them in
as Source/WebKit/zebkit, and they are named in SourcesCocoa.txt like any
other source of the framework.

The rest is where WebKit has to tell the endpoint something. A WKWebView
reports to the delegates its application gave it, and has one of each, so
the endpoint cannot be a delegate. It is told from the places the delegates
are called from instead:

- WKWebView: a view was set up, a view is going. Each is a page a CDP
  client can drive.
- NavigationState: the main frame's loads (started, committed, finished,
  failed), the end of the page's process, and authentication challenges,
  which is how a certificate error arrives and where a client's request to
  ignore them is granted.
- UIDelegate: script dialogs and beforeunload, which a client answers when
  one is attached to the page; file choosers a client has announced files
  for; a page closing itself; and a page opening a window, for which the
  endpoint makes a view when the application makes none.

An application's delegates are asked as before in every case the endpoint
does not take, and it takes none while no client is attached.

